      "handoff_review": "One reviewer-controlled deduplication product: normalized snapshots, confidence-bearing matching and conservative clustering feed persistent review; confirmed apply recomputes plans and checks schema/row/decision hashes under a document lock before one Sheets batchUpdate with audit. Low-confidence edges do not merge core components. Railway authenticates scan jobs and persists reviewable progress; Apps Script/sidebar and local XLSX CLI share engine contracts while actual workbook deployment remains separate. README privacy sentence claiming no fetch is stale relative to its own owned-backend introduction, docs/BACKEND.md and remoteScan.ts; retain no third-party matching/no remote sidebar assets, not a fictitious no-network runtime. Exact build, launcher, fixture and runtime support paths are included; their presence is not independent behavioral proof. Hosted Railway execution, real Sheets service credentials and local-versus-remote review/apply separation remain unverified; owned-remote-scan remains accepted and unbound.",
